---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Terms of Service | SolarSite Texas"
  description="Terms of service and operational dispatch agreements for SolarSite Texas."
>
  <section class="section section-dark page-hero">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <h1 class="page-title">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="color: #94A3B8;">Last updated: August 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="legal-content card-technical" style="padding: var(--space-8); line-height: 1.7;">
        <h3>1. Service Coordination Scope</h3>
        <p>SolarSite Texas acts as a professional coordination and quality-assurance platform connecting Solar EPCs, dealers, and contractors with vetted independent field site surveyors.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">2. Scheduling & Availability</h3>
        <p>Site surveys are scheduled according to selected requested availability and earliest open time slots, subject to weather conditions, customer property access, and safe climbing environments.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">3. Deliverable Acceptance & QA</h3>
        <p>All delivered survey packages undergo internal desk QA. If an essential photo or measurement specified in our 36-photo standard is missing or unreadable due to surveyor error, a re-dispatch will be conducted at no additional charge to the EPC.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">4. Limitation of Liability</h3>
        <p>Survey data and preliminary electrical calculations are provided to assist the contractor’s licensed Professional Engineer (PE) and CAD draftspersons. Final structural and electrical designs remain the legal responsibility of the licensed engineer of record and installing contractor.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
